    "description":  "\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eDescription of PROTEiCA project survey\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eThe PROTEiCA survey is part of the academic research project \u003ci\u003eProtest, Learning, and Political Change\u003c/i\u003e (PROTEiCA). This project investigates the relationship between individual protest experiences, learning processes, and changes in political attitudes. The study examines these dynamics both among individuals who actively participate in protests and those who experience them indirectly through media coverage.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp dir=\"ltr\"\u003eThe survey aims to generate rigorous data to enhance our understanding of political systems, employing scientific methods to explore social phenomena related to protest. Participation in this survey is crucial for advancing knowledge that can contribute to improving political systems.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eIncluded Materials:\u003c/h3\u003e\u003col\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eSurvey Questionnaire\u003c/b\u003e:\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eAvailable in both English and Spanish (original version).\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eData Files\u003c/b\u003e:\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThe original dataset provided in two formats: \u003ccode\u003e.CSV\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003e.DTA\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eAvailable in both English and Spanish (original version).\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eContributors:\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eManuel Jiménez-Sánchez \u003c/b\u003ecarried out the conceptualization, methodological design, validation and data curation tasks as well as funding acquisition and project administration.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eMarta Fraile \u003c/b\u003eand \u003cb\u003eJosep Lobera\u003c/b\u003e, as members of the research team for the PROTEiCA project, contributed to the survey design conception.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eDaniel Romero-\u003c/b\u003e\u003cb\u003ePortillo\u003c/b\u003e conducted the data curation tasks for making the raw research data available.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e",
